---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const schema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"name": "Technical Foundations",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Tatkraft Marketing" },
	"areaServed": ["NZ", "AU"],
	"description": "Schema, structured data and crawler access — the technical foundations most sites get wrong without realising it."
};
---

<Layout
	title="Technical SEO & AI Crawler Access"
	description="Technical SEO, schema and AI crawler access — the technical foundations most sites get wrong without realising it."
	schema={schema}
>
	<h1>Technical Foundations</h1>
	<p class="tagline">The plumbing that decides whether AI systems can even read you.</p>

	<p>
		Before any content strategy matters, AI crawlers and search engines need to be
		able to access, parse and trust your site. A surprising number of sites are
		quietly blocking the crawlers they're trying to be found by, or missing the
		structured data that tells a machine what a page actually is.
	</p>
	<p>
		This is technical SEO — still the same discipline it's always been, now doing
		double duty for the AI crawlers and language models behind AEO and GEO as well
		as traditional search engines.
	</p>

	<h2>What this covers</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Schema and structured data markup</li>
		<li>AI crawler access and permissions (llms.txt, robots.txt)</li>
		<li>Technical SEO audits</li>
		<li>Indexation and crawlability fixes</li>
		<li>Site speed and Core Web Vitals</li>
		<li>Site migrations without losing visibility</li>
		<li>Ongoing structured data testing and monitoring</li>
	</ul>

	<a class="cta" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
</Layout>
